      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Charming Traditional Stone Cottage Overlooking the Atlantic Ocean\r\n\r\nKilbaha is a delightful and unspoilt fishing village situated at the western tip of the Loop Head Peninsula, renowned for its rugged coastline, spectacular scenery and relaxed coastal atmosphere. The property is ideally positioned for those seeking a peaceful retreat while remaining within easy reach of the many attractions and amenities of West Clare.\r\n\r\nSituated in a truly spectacular coastal setting on the outskirts of the picturesque fishing village of Kilbaha, this charming three-bedroom detached stone-built cottage offers a wonderful blend of traditional character and modern convenience, complemented by breathtaking views across the Atlantic Ocean.\r\n\r\nSet on a generous 0.5-acre site, the property enjoys an enviable position along Ireland's Wild Atlantic Way, on the scenic west coast of County Clare. The uninterrupted coastal outlook provides a magnificent backdrop, with ever-changing sea and sky views that can be enjoyed from the property and its surrounding grounds.\r\n\r\nThe cottage retains much of its traditional charm and character, while modern conveniences have been thoughtfully introduced over the years. The accommodation comprises a front porch, kitchen, living room, lounge/dining room, three bedrooms and a bathroom. The property benefits from a dual heating system incorporating oil-fired central heating and solid fuel, providing flexibility and comfort throughout the year.\r\n\r\nOutside, the generous site offers excellent space and privacy, with the property's elevated coastal setting providing breathtaking panoramic views of the Atlantic Ocean.\r\n\r\nThis is a rare opportunity to acquire a traditional coastal cottage in an outstanding location, offering character, generous grounds and truly magnificent Atlantic Ocean views."
      },
